secubox-certs (1.0.2-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * L'unite retire sa socket perimee via `ExecStartPre=+/bin/rm`.
    /run/secubox porte le bit collant : on n'y delie que ce qu'on possede,
    et une socket laissee par un autre utilisateur rend le demarrage
    impossible — le service echoue, redemarre, echoue encore, en silence.
  * `RuntimeDirectory=secubox` retire : systemd efface le contenu d'un
    RuntimeDirectory au redemarrage, et ce repertoire est partage par ~95
    unites. Une seule qui le declare emporte les sockets des autres.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:35:59 +0200

secubox-certs (1.0.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * SECURITY: the API had NO authentication — `Depends` was imported and
    require_jwt never called. Verified in production: GET /list returned 200 to
    an unauthenticated LAN client through the full HAProxy chain, and POST
    /issue and DELETE /revoke sat on the same router. Any LAN device could
    issue or revoke the box's TLS certificates.
    Every route now requires a session; /health stays public for probes;
    /issue, /renew, /renew-all and /revoke additionally require role=admin.
    (ref #942)

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:30:00 +0200

